==English==

===Etymology===
Prefix form of {{m|en|prest}}, perhaps after Italian {{m|it|imprestare}}, or perhaps from a misunderstand of the phrase ''in prest''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɪmpɹɛst/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-imprest.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[advance]] of [[fund]]s, especially to a [[government]] service or [[employee]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#* '''1977''', {{w|John Le Carré}}, ''The Honourable Schoolboy'', Folio Society 2010, p. 240:
#*: Calling on Lacon at the Cabinet Office to deliver the Circus's monthly '''imprest''' account for his inspection, he had been astonished to see Sam emerging from his private office, joking easily with Lacon and Saul Enderby of the Foreign Office.

====Translations====
